.TH DT-MOVE 1 "August 2026" "dirtoo tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dt-move \- move files into a directory (dirtoo / dirops)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dt-move
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.B \-t
.I DIR
.I FILE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Move one or more files or directories into a target directory.
The legacy two-argument form
.B dt-move
.I from to
is
.B not
supported; always pass
.BR \-t .
For renaming a single path to a new name, use
.BR dt-rename (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target\-directory " " \fIDIR\fR
Destination directory (required).
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-relative
Preserve path prefix under
.IR DIR .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Plan only; do not modify the filesystem.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print each successful move.
.TP
.BR \-Y ", " \-\-always
Overwrite on conflict.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-never
Skip on conflict.
.TP
.BR \-\-conflict=\fIPOLICY\fR
.IR fail ,
.IR overwrite ,
.IR rename ,
or
.IR skip .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
.TQ
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dt-move -t /tmp/out photo.jpg notes.txt
dt-move -R -t /backup home/user/docs/a.pdf
dt-move -n -v --conflict=rename -t ./dest ./*.png
.fi
.SH CONFLICT POLICIES
When the destination path already exists, the following policies apply
(via
.BR \-\-conflict
or shorthand flags where available):
.TP
.B fail
Abort that item with an error (default for most tools).
.TP
.B overwrite
Replace the existing destination.
.TP
.B rename
Choose a unique name such as
.I stem\ (N).ext
.
.TP
.B skip
Leave the destination unchanged and continue.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dirtoo (1),
.BR dt-copy (1),
.BR dt-move (1),
.BR dt-rename (1),
.BR dt-rm (1),
.BR dt-mkdir (1),
.BR dt-filter (1)
